- column  Code
- column  Variant
- column  Wire code
- column  Meaning
- column  Resolution
- row  `↯/s.127.1.1`  `NoSuchElement`  `no such element`  The element addressed by the action was not present in the DOM.  Verify the locator strategy and target; wait for the element to appear before acting on it.
- row  `↯/s.127.1.2`  `StaleElement`  `stale element reference`  The element was previously located but has since been removed from or replaced in the DOM.  Re-locate the element after navigation or DOM mutation before retrying.
- row  `↯/s.127.1.3`  `NoSuchWindow`  `no such window`  The window or tab handle referenced by the action does not exist.  Confirm the window handle is current; switch to a valid window before acting.
- row  `↯/s.127.1.4`  `JavascriptError`  `javascript error`  A script evaluated by the WebDriver threw an exception.  Inspect the script and the supplied `detail` for the underlying JavaScript exception.
- row  `↯/s.127.1.5`  `ScriptTimeout`  `script timeout`  An asynchronous script did not complete within the configured timeout.  Raise the script timeout, or fix the script so that it resolves promptly.
- row  `↯/s.127.1.6`  `Timeout`  `timeout`  The WebDriver operation timed out before completion.  Raise the relevant timeout, or fix the page so that the awaited condition can be met.
- row  `↯/s.127.1.7`  `UnknownCommand`  `unknown command`  The WebDriver does not recognise the command issued.  Confirm the WebDriver version supports the action; upgrade the driver if necessary.
- row  `↯/s.127.1.8`  `Other`  *(any unrecognized code)*  The WebDriver reported an error code that does not map to one of the other cases. The original code is captured in the `Other(code)` parameter.  Consult the W3C WebDriver specification, or the driver's own documentation, for the reported code.
- row  `↯/s.127.1.9`  `ElementClickIntercepted`  `element click intercepted`  Another element would receive the click — typically an overlay, a modal or a sticky header.  Scroll the target into view, dismiss the obscuring element, or click through the actions API.
- row  `↯/s.127.1.10`  `ElementNotInteractable`  `element not interactable`  The element is in the DOM but cannot receive the interaction.  Wait until the element is displayed and enabled; check it is not zero-sized or `pointer-events: none`.
- row  `↯/s.127.1.11`  `InsecureCertificate`  `insecure certificate`  Navigation was blocked because the page was served with an untrusted certificate.  Request the `acceptInsecureCerts` capability when the session is created.
- row  `↯/s.127.1.12`  `InvalidArgument`  `invalid argument`  An argument to the command was not of the type or in the range the specification requires.  Check the argument against the specification for that command.
- row  `↯/s.127.1.13`  `InvalidCookieDomain`  `invalid cookie domain`  A cookie was set for a domain other than the current document's.  Navigate to the cookie's domain before setting it.
- row  `↯/s.127.1.14`  `InvalidElementState`  `invalid element state`  The element's state forbids the command — clearing a non-editable element, for instance.  Check the element is editable, or use script execution instead.
- row  `↯/s.127.1.15`  `InvalidSelector`  `invalid selector`  The locator was not valid for its strategy.  Check the CSS selector or XPath expression.
- row  `↯/s.127.1.16`  `InvalidSessionId`  `invalid session id`  The session is no longer active: it was deleted, or the browser terminated.  Open a fresh session; do not retain a session handle beyond its block.
- row  `↯/s.127.1.17`  `MoveTargetOutOfBounds`  `move target out of bounds`  A pointer action addressed coordinates outside the viewport.  Scroll the target into view, or use element-relative pointer origins.
- row  `↯/s.127.1.18`  `NoSuchAlert`  `no such alert`  An alert command was issued while no user prompt was open.  Check for an open prompt before accepting, dismissing or reading it.
- row  `↯/s.127.1.19`  `NoSuchCookie`  `no such cookie`  No cookie of that name is associated with the current document.  Check the name, the document's domain, and the cookie's path.
- row  `↯/s.127.1.20`  `NoSuchFrame`  `no such frame`  The frame handle or index referenced by the action does not exist.  Check the frame index or element; switch back to the top-level context first.
- row  `↯/s.127.1.21`  `NoSuchShadowRoot`  `no such shadow root`  The element does not host a shadow root.  Check the element hosts an open shadow root; closed roots are not reachable.
- row  `↯/s.127.1.22`  `DetachedShadowRoot`  `detached shadow root`  The shadow root was located but its host has since left the DOM.  Re-locate the host element and its shadow root after DOM mutation.
- row  `↯/s.127.1.23`  `SessionNotCreated`  `session not created`  The driver could not start a session, commonly a browser/driver version mismatch or a missing browser binary.  Check the driver matches the installed browser; check the requested capabilities.
- row  `↯/s.127.1.24`  `UnableToSetCookie`  `unable to set cookie`  The driver could not set the cookie.  Check the cookie's domain, path, `secure` and `sameSite` attributes against the current document.
- row  `↯/s.127.1.25`  `UnableToCaptureScreen`  `unable to capture screen`  The screenshot could not be taken.  Check the element has a non-empty rendered area, and that the window is not minimized.
- row  `↯/s.127.1.26`  `UnexpectedAlertOpen`  `unexpected alert open`  A user prompt was open when a command that requires none was issued.  Accept or dismiss the prompt, or set the `unhandledPromptBehavior` capability.
- row  `↯/s.127.1.27`  `UnknownError`  `unknown error`  The driver reported a failure it could not classify. This is also raised when a driver replies with a body that is not the W3C error object at all — a crashed driver, or an interposed proxy — in which case `detail` is the raw body.  Inspect `detail` and `browserStacktrace`; check the driver's own log.
- row  `↯/s.127.1.28`  `UnknownMethod`  `unknown method`  The command exists but does not support the HTTP method used.  Check the command's method against the specification.
- row  `↯/s.127.1.29`  `UnsupportedOperation`  `unsupported operation`  The driver does not implement the command.  Check the driver's conformance; some commands, such as printing to PDF, are not universal.
